you have this one life to live and you  can either choose to be a spectator and  follow other people's awesome lives  or get out there and do the work that it  takes every single day  to better your life and better the lives  of others in the process  which will you choose  hey everyone welcome to yessi tv where  we talk about minimalism as more than  just decluttering  physical items from your life today's  video is specifically requested and i  hope that it will be beneficial to those  of you  who have seen some of my other videos on  digital minimalism such as  why i quit social media or how to break  your phone addiction  but it's for those of you who have  either quit or intend to and want to but  just can't help but keep coming back i  have a disclaimer before we  begin though i found out through a  couple viewers on some of my previous  videos that youtube is actually  considered social media  so upfront i apologize for having given  any misinformation  i did not know that youtube was  considered social media  but to that person who commented that i  be  beat needed to talk about how youtube  can be bad and cause depression and  anxiety  to you i say i am not the person to talk  about that because youtube has made a  positive impact in my life  youtube has allowed me to stalk people  like oprah tony robbins dave ramsey  basically i can learn from a lot of  people that i don't even have to know  in person and to the mommy youtubers you  saved my life when i was a new mom  so youtube has been beneficial for me  and i hope that what we talk about here  is beneficial in some sort of way  so just now so that we're all on the  same page that i am talking about  websites like facebook instagram twitter  those kinds of websites  not youtube all that being said on to  what you came here for  okay so you're sitting on your couch  you've quit social media you have your  reasons for why you did it  and you're thinking of opening these  apps again because  you just don't know what to do with  yourself guys this is withdrawal  having worked in an icu for a few years  i know that the first few days to weeks  of a withdrawal from alcohol or drugs  are crucial and can actually be  life-threatening okay  you're not going to die from not  checking websites like facebook  but your brain doesn't know the  difference it's used to that dopamine  spike that feeling of reward when you  check it  so it wants you to stop being  uncomfortable and do what makes it feel  good your brain is designed to save you  from saber-toothed tigers and any sign  of danger  this is why it's so darn difficult to do  the little things you know you should be  doing  such as finishing that assignment that  you have to or  getting up at 5am to finish that youtube  video  so tip number one is know your triggers  and have barriers for them  some of you mentioned triggers in the  comments such as fear of missing out  or boredom and first of all it's great  that you know what these temptations are  for you because  that way you can know what to attack to  make it harder to go back in the first  place  a few things that you can try for this  are to actually delete the accounts  instead of just unfollowing or  unsubscribing  this makes it a little bit harder to  actually go back but there are actually  apps out there that can help you stop  using these sorts of apps and accounts  such as  stay on task break free and what was the  other one off time  i've never actually used these apps  myself so i'm not telling you to use  these specific  ones but just know that these apps are  out there if you feel like the urge is  too strong to bear  next thing i would recommend for you is  to focus on  day by day instead of this long period  of time  don't tell yourself i'm going to quit  social media for a month or for a year  that's too stressful tell yourself today  i'm going to choose  to spend time with my family instead or  today  i'm going to work on that project that  i've been putting off for  a while today i'm going to focus on  improving myself  make the decision each day tip number  two is set goals for yourself  it's hard to find motivation for  something when you don't know why you're  doing it in the first place or where you  want to be in the future  since adopting a more minimalist  lifestyle one of the things that i love  to do is to set goals for myself  and i actually began by asking myself  where do i want to see myself in five to  ten years from now  i actually write out my goals on a  notebook and i have social goals health  goals financial goals and spiritual  goals  at the beginning of the year i write  down a list of major big goals that i  want to accomplish  and then i kind of break it down to make  it easier for myself to actually  get to those goals by setting monthly  and sometimes weekly goals  that i can keep tracking this helps me  to keep motivated and it gives me an  idea of  where i want to be in life and how to  actually get there  this way i feel like i'm actually  working towards something instead of  just  doing for the sake of doing or living  for the sake of living  so if you quit social media don't just  do it just because  ask yourself now what and set goals for  yourself  tip number three is strengthen your  relationships  in two months i will actually be on six  years now without social media  but one of the things that helped me a  lot during that time was that i was  trying to overcome a battle with social  anxiety  so i was intentionally trying to develop  stronger relationships with more  positive people  i intentionally made the purpose of  calling people and it started to call  people more often  and for someone with social anxiety this  was so extremely difficult  because it's not like when you're  sending a text or you're typing on a  computer  and you actually get to think about what  you're going to say before you say it  at the time i was also very involved in  my church and participating in events  and constantly meeting new people  i realized that i'm filming this in the  middle of a pandemic so we have to get a  little bit creative with the way that we  socialize but do  place more emphasis on this humans crave  connection we need it  this is often why these sites are so  addicting because we  think we have these connections with  people when a lot of times their  connections are really very superficial  so many times i've seen married couples  at restaurants each glued to their phone  and not ever really talking to each  other  or how many times have you seen either  parents or their kids  on their phone not really talking to  each other at a restaurant or how many  people actually  sit down and have dinner and shared  together laugh together  tell stories together at dinner time so  think of the people that you value in  your life and find ways to build a  deeper connection with them  tip number four is to try adopting new  hobbies or activities that bring you joy  sometimes the best way to beat an old  habit is by replacing it with a new one  i remember when my husband quit video  games it was very hard for him initially  but he used that extra time to spend  more quality time with my daughter and i  and get back to his old hobbies of  construction and building furniture  if you feel like you don't really have  hobbies or the hobbies you used to have  don't really bring you joy anymore it  could be several things  depression can definitely be a cause you  might not feel like you have the time or  the money to do so  or you might just not be trying new  things maybe try going to a place that  you've never  been to before try adopting a new hobby  or try meeting new people  our brains start aging the moment we  stop learning  trying new things and having new  experiences can help you develop more  creativity  and possibly give you the motivation you  need to take on new projects  tip number five look for ways to serve  others  i feel like this tip might sound cheesy  but looking back at my life the moments  when i felt the most empty inside  when i felt like i questioned what the  point of living even was  why i was even alive in the first place  was when i was more focused on myself  and what was wrong with me or what i was  missing and what i didn't have  but when i was finally able to shift my  focus to that outside myself and think  of  others and that other people are  suffering or going through worse  situations than i am  then it gave me a sense of purpose  because if i  get to complain that i'm bored about not  having social media then it means that i  have the time  to work on improving the lives of others  before i say this  let me be very clear i do not say this  to glorify myself but it is important  that i share it with you  before becoming a nurse i volunteered at  a homeless shelter i visited the sick i  remember  actually going to the hospital on  christmas day and visiting the people  who didn't have family members there  with them  i volunteered at hospital fundraisers i  volunteered at my church regularly  i did all of these things but they  brought me such  joy and satisfaction even though some  people would say it's a waste of time  because those moments when i got to  touch other people's lives  were the things that actually motivated  me gave me life and made me feel  that i had a purpose and sometimes the  hobbies that are meant to bring us joy  don't give us the same satisfaction the  sense of fulfillment and purpose  so if you are sitting at home bored  because you don't have these apps  anymore  i encourage you to get out of your  bubble and look for ways to serve in  your community  i assure you the satisfaction you would  get is much better than if you were to  just  stay on your sofa and do nothing tip  number six  practice more gratitude if you still  can't seem to find joy or fulfillment  from  spending more time with the ones that  you love serving others or trying  different hobbies  then maybe you could use a little more  gratitude in your life  this simple daily practice of listing  the things that you're grateful for can  help you become a more positive  individual  that sees opportunities rather than  problems  when you're grateful for the things that  you have you don't have time  to focus on the things that you don't  have or that you're missing out on  so focus on adding a little more  gratitude to your daily life  and lastly tip number seven constantly  feed yourself  stop i'm not talking about the  refrigerator i'm talking on a spiritual  and  intellectual level when i quit social  media i was so worried about what i was  going to do with my time without it  until i realized what i was doing was a  waste of time anyway  so i began to adopt more positive habits  instead and for me this included a lot  of spiritual growth as well  but i also did other things such as i  started to cook more and eat healthier  i started to exercise regularly which i  really need to get back to  i journaled i read i started listening  to more inspirational youtube videos i  was constantly  feeding my mind with positivity and  things that were going to help me become  better  each day i also made a conscious effort  to start  having a less association with the  negative nancies in my life  and start having more positive  relationships as well if you had a good  enough reason to stop social media in  the first place then don't just stop  there  let this one decision become a domino  effect of positive changes in your life  use this time to practice new habits  that will help you become a better  version of yourself tomorrow  than you are today and let me know in  the comments  what new habits you plan to adopt today  that's it for today guys if you like  this video please give it a thumbs up  and subscribe so you won't miss when i  post a new video  i thank you so much for watching and as  always if you have any other ideas  please leave them in the comments i love  to learn from you  can't wait to hear from you bye

